          "The customs change deserves the detail, because it is the one fact on this page with a date that matters more than a price. For years, Section 321 of the Tariff Act of 1930 let shipments worth $800 or less enter the United States duty-free. Executive Order 14324 suspended that treatment for every country effective August 29, 2025. CBP then made the suspension indefinite through interim final rules published June 24, 2026 (91 FR 37789 for shipments other than mail, 91 FR 37801 for mail), and the One Big Beautiful Bill Act repeals the exemption from the statute entirely effective July 1, 2027. The practical meaning is simple: a parcel worth $1 owes the same treatment as a parcel worth $799, and every shipment now needs an entry with a tariff classification. Check your own customs authority's current rules before you order, and treat a shop still advertising the $800 rule as live as one that has not updated its advice since August 2025."
